Adds a compiler-time debugger via `pragma(breakpoint)`

When a `pragma breakpoint` statement is analyzed during semantic, compilation is paused and presents a debugger console to the user mimicing GDB/LLDB

Currently, the debugger supports:

* backtrace -- show the nested scopes that the breakpoint occurs in, analgous to a call stack
* members -- show the symbols in a specified scope
* continue -- end the debugging session, keep compiling
